  promptText: Rare heritage seeds used in my signature dishes originated from elders
    without consent. Returning them restores cultural rights but may bankrupt my
    business and displace staff; retaining them keeps incomes but perpetuates appropriation.
  leftAnswer: Returning seeds honours elders and repairs long-term cultural trust.
  rightAnswer: Keeping the business preserves jobs and income for many families today.
